   largest 2.61 mF, smallest 1.67 mF; the soft start's own draw 8.6 / 6.5 / 5.6 % of 4.80 A at 9 / 12 / 13.8 V; the bleed's tau
   0.20 to 0.35 s, 0.64 to 1.17 s to release; the restart ring 14.3 A (82 % of L1's 17.5 A typical Isat at 25 C), 0.82 mJ: as recorded
   The restart figure is first order: lossless, constant inductance, not saturation aware; the ballast's damping is not credited

9. PREDICATES
   consistency: the derivation meets every recorded dense can figure within 0.02 A and the re-review's point within 0.0005 A: yes
   consistency: the loop model meets the recorded margins within the stated tolerances: yes
   convergence: on the finer source grids every can figure of the drawn node moves by less than the rule's margin: yes
   the full enumeration of the second fix-up's node equals the search's maximum and counts the record's sets over the rating: yes
   B1: the check's counterexample reproduces, 2.8546 A on its 204 / 816 kHz coincidence against its 2.7375 A in mean square: yes
   B2: the check's ESL counterexample reproduces, 3.5870 A with the siblings at 3.5 nH plus the layout's 0.5 nH, a corner whose can parameters the decision box spans: yes
   B3: the envelope covers the specified row's low corner carried to RT, under the record's 180.3 kHz: yes
   the drawn bank does NOT meet 2.8 A at the 2:1 spread at either outcome on the corrected model: yes
   B2: without a resistance floor no can count bounds the per-can current (the drawn six and eight cans both read over 10 A): yes
   B2: the selected ballast meets the rule at both outcomes on the independent box, every source combination and coincidence: yes
   the selected bank's worst moves by under the rule's margin with 120 harmonics and with the coincidence lines sampled four times finer: yes
   the rating applies unmodified in frequency: every harmonic at or above 172 kHz, where the sheet's correction is 1.00: yes
   the ballast's own loss is under a tenth of the sheet's 3 W: yes
   the loop keeps PM >= 50 deg, GM >= 10 dB, |1+T| >= 0.5, every crossover under its ceilings and the impedance under its bound with the ballast, the sheet's C band and B3's envelope at L4-E6's R12 12 mOhm, loads to the highest permitted current, default and widened bands: yes
   ORDER: with the drawn R12 the ballast takes the widened gain margin under 10 dB even at the record's loads, so it goes in with L4-E6's R12 (the draft refuses the tree otherwise): yes
   the cold limit: the drawn bank on the drawn R12 misses GM >= 10 dB there as well, and the round's change (R12 12 mOhm with the ballast) holds the cans' ESR at least as far as the drawn circuit does, every flip point above the +20 C endurance limit: yes
   the first-order consequences reproduce the generator's recorded soft-start draw, bleed tau, node maximum and restart ring: yes
